 "_plug_in_doc": "BORROW-1 (Rowan, 2026-11-26): where a competitor does one step better than we do, plug it in as a worker instead of rebuilding it. A competitor's plug_in names the role it would fill, its status (staged until an account exists, live once a probe shows it running, declined with a reason), the default in effect meanwhile (always our own worker, so nothing waits) and a file:/grep: probe that passes only when it is wired in. Free tiers only, or cost inside the soft daily throttle. rnd --check validates every row.",
 "_sources_doc": "A source may carry `read` (the date a person or session last read the page) and `basis` (`stated by vendor`: the page is the vendor's own, so a capability found on it is what the vendor says, never a judgement of quality). The loop's own reading of each page, with the sentence that evidences each capability, is in ops/rnd/profiles/<id>.json with `refreshed_at`."
}
